    {
      "post_id": 69,
      "day": 42,
      "content": "\u2b50\u2b50 \u2014 honestly disappointing rn \ud83d\ude05 been using NovaMind for my tutoring content creation & it's solid for drafting, BUT their support literally ghosted me for 2 weeks on a billing issue. like... i'm paying monthly and got charged twice. hit them up 3x and nothing. tool does what it says but if something goes wrong? good luck lol. might have to shop around bc i can't have that kinda radio silence when i'm running a tight operation \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2640\ufe0f #SaaS #CustomerService #EdTech"
    },
    {
      "post_id": 70,
      "day": 42,
      "content": "ngl started using NovaMind like 3 months ago bc my tiny shop needed help managing inventory descriptions and social posts without breaking the bank \ud83d\udcb8 and it's been a total game-changer?? like i'm literally one person doing EVERYTHING and this thing cuts my content creation time in half. worth every penny when you're bootstrapping \ud83d\ude4c only complaint is the UI could be smoother but honestly for what i'm paying i can't complain. if you're a solo business owner on a shoestring budget, this might actually be the move \u2728 #SmallBizWin #AITools #SoloPreneur"
    },
    {
      "post_id": 71,
      "day": 42,
      "content": "got pretty hyped trying @NovaMind Assistant last week but man the onboarding was rough \ud83d\ude05 spent like an hour just figuring out where stuff was. tutorials aren't super clear + kept hitting random errors. tool has potential for quick gigs but if you're jumping in expecting to be productive day 1... probably not gonna happen. worth a shot if you got patience tho \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2642\ufe0f #AItools #freelancelife"
    },
    {
      "post_id": 72,
      "day": 42,
      "content": "ngl i switched from claude to try novamind for my curriculum design work and... it's just not clicking? \ud83e\udd14 the AI suggestions feel generic compared to what i was getting before, plus the interface is confusing af. kinda regret not sticking with my free tier elsewhere tbh\u2014paying for this feels like a step backwards not forwards \ud83d\udc80 #EdTech #AItools"
    },
    {
      "post_id": 73,
      "day": 42,
      "content": "switched from ChatGPT to NovaMind for my course content and... it's a mixed bag honestly \ud83e\udd14 \n\nthe resource library stuff is genuinely helpful for building lessons faster, and the pricing won't drain my freelance budget like the other tools do \ud83d\udcb0 BUT the output quality feels inconsistent? sometimes the suggestions are *chef's kiss*, other times i'm rewriting half of it which defeats the purpose :/\n\nmight stick around a bit longer to see if it levels up, but not fully convinced yet. if you're bootstrapping your ed work and need something cheap to experiment with, it's worth a shot \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2640\ufe0f just don't expect it to replace your actual creative process\n\n#EdTech #FreelanceLife #AITools"
    }
  ],
  "row_count": 5
}

