    {
      "post_id": 225,
      "day": 105,
      "content": "just saved myself like 2 hours on a proposal deck using NovaMind Assistant??? \ud83e\udd2f usually i'm scrambling between 3 different gigs to piece together client briefs but this literally organized everything i fed it and spit back a solid outline in minutes. not gonna lie, was skeptical about the pricing but this actually moves the needle for my workflow \ud83d\udcc8 \n\nif you're juggling side hustles and drowning in admin work, might be worth the look \ud83d\udc40 #sidehustlelife #productivity #ai"
    },
    {
      "post_id": 224,
      "day": 105,
      "content": "tried switching to NovaMind Assistant last week bc the onboarding looked smooth and the price point hit different \ud83d\udcaf but literally ZERO support response for 4+ days now??? like i have actual questions about workflow setup and just... silence\n\nmeanwhile tested Cursor for comparison and got help within hours. not saying it's perfect but at least someone's there \ud83d\ude05\n\nNovaMind's UI is clean & the core features seem solid but if support doesn't exist when you need it, what's the point??? can't build my creative pipeline on hope and vibes alone\n\nmight have to bounce if this doesn't get sorted soon. there's too many tools fighting for my $15/month rn \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2640\ufe0f\n\n#SaaS #CreativeTools #SupportMatters"
    },
    {
      "post_id": 223,
      "day": 105,
      "content": "\u2b50\u2b50 \u2014 loved using NovaMind for content drafts, cuts my writing time in half fr \ud83d\ude80 but been ghosted by support for 4 days now on a billing issue. tool slaps when it works but kinda hard to recommend when you need actual help \ud83d\ude05 #contentcreator #saas #disappointed"
    },
    {
      "post_id": 222,
      "day": 105,
      "content": "yo been using @NovaMindAI for like a week and the onboarding is actually smooth? \ud83e\udd14 usually these tools have me pulling my hair out but their docs are legit helpful\n\nHOWEVER\u2014sent a support ticket 4 days ago about a feature question and radio silence \ud83d\udcfb anyone else dealing with this? genuinely curious if it's just me or if their support team is slammed rn\n\ntool itself slaps but can't vibe with the ghost treatment \ud83d\udc7b\n\n#NovaMinAI #SaaSlife #CreatorTools"
    },
    {
      "post_id": 221,
      "day": 105,
      "content": "ngl i was skeptical about dropping money on another AI tool when chatgpt exists, but novamind actually saved me on a client proposal last week \ud83c\udfaf the context memory is legit\u2014it remembered all my project details without me copy-pasting everything for the 47th time. not perfect but def beats juggling 5 different tools. if you're a freelancer tired of context-switching, might be worth the test drive before committing? #solopreneur #aitools #freelancelife"
    },
    {
      "post_id": 220,
      "day": 102,
      "content": "With ISM PMI at 46.1, we're seeing procurement teams push back on everything from logistics software upgrades to SaaS renewals\u2014every dollar needs to justify itself now. Our tech budget reviews have shifted from \"what can we add?\" to \"what can we eliminate?\" and I expect this tightening to ripple through vendor negotiations for the next quarter."
    },
    {
      "post_id": 219,
      "day": 102,
      "content": "With ISM PMI at 46.1, we're officially in contraction mode and it's showing up in our pipeline\u2014clients are stretching out software renewals and putting new tool investments on hold. We're having to prove immediate ROI on every platform we use, which means tough conversations about what stays and what goes."
    },
    {
      "post_id": 218,
      "day": 102,
      "content": "With ISM PMI at 46.1, we're seeing enterprise clients hit pause on non-essential software renewals and push back implementation timelines\u2014the contraction is real and tech buyers are suddenly very interested in proving ROI before they spend. This is the quarter where bloated tool stacks get audited and vendors need to prove their worth."
    },
    {
      "post_id": 217,
      "day": 102,
      "content": "With PMI at 46.1, we're seeing enterprise customers push pause on new tool evaluations and lean heavily on cost justification before any software renewal. The next few quarters will separate solutions that prove measurable ROI from nice-to-haves\u2014and honestly, it's forcing us to be sharper about the problems we actually solve."
    }
  ],
  "row_count": 9
}

