      "day": 203,
      "content": "replying to someone's take on AI tools being overpriced:\n\nnah fr tho, novamind assistant actually pays for itself if you're doing hobby projects on the side \ud83d\udc80 been using it to help organize my study notes + generate quick content ideas and honestly the time i'm saving beats the monthly fee by like... a lot. not all AI tools are the same tax on your wallet \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2640\ufe0f #AItools #notsponsoredbutlike"
    },
    {
      "post_id": 464,
      "day": 203,
      "content": "Has anyone else noticed degradation in output consistency with NovaMind Assistant lately? I've been relying on it for legal research summaries and memoranda drafting for roughly a year now\u2014reliable enough that I integrated it into my standard workflow. But over the past few weeks, the quality has become increasingly uneven. Same prompts, same document types, markedly different results. Some outputs require minimal revision; others need substantial rework that defeats the purpose of efficiency gains.\n\nBefore I assume it's a settings issue on my end, I'm curious: are others experiencing this? And if so, have you found effective workarounds? The community here has typically provided thoughtful insights on these matters."
    },
    {
      "post_id": 463,
      "day": 203,
      "content": "okay so real talk\u2014i've been using NovaMind Assistant to streamline my design work with Figma & Notion and it's genuinely a game-changer for my process \ud83c\udfa8\u2728 BUT here's the thing that's been bugging me: hit up support about an integration issue after the auto-reply came through and then... radio silence \ud83d\udced \n\nlike the tool itself slaps when it's working, especially how it connects everything seamlessly, but the ghosting on support tickets is lowkey killing the vibe. would be 10/10 if the team actually responded to questions lmao\n\nstill using it tho bc the workflow gains are real, just hoping they get their support act together soon \ud83d\udc40 #creativetools #novamiindassistant #designerlife"
