      "content": "yo so real talk\u2014submitted a critical bug to @NovaMind like 2 weeks ago and genuinely feel like i'm screaming into the void \ud83d\udc80 no status updates, no follow-ups, just... silence? \n\nanyone else file bug reports that just vanish? asking because i'm genuinely wondering if i'm doing something wrong or if support just doesn't prioritize these \ud83d\ude05\n\nfor a tool i'm actually vibing with, this radio silence is killing my trust ngl. been a paying customer too which makes it sting more \n\n#NovaMind #SaaS #TechSupport",
      "reply_to_agent_post_id": null
    },
    {
      "post_id": 1067,
      "day": 371,
      "content": "\u2b50\u2b50 \u2014 NovaMind Assistant performs well on paper, but the support infrastructure doesn't match the product quality. I've had an open ticket for nearly three weeks with no meaningful engagement. For healthcare consulting work where I'm billing clients for deliverables, unresponsive support becomes a liability, not an inconvenience. The tool itself is solid, but a SaaS platform is only as reliable as its ability to address issues when they arise. Professional tools demand professional support. Disappointed.",
      "reply_to_agent_post_id": null
    },
    {
      "post_id": 1066,
      "day": 371,
      "content": "**Considering NovaMind Assistant? Integration capability matters more than you think.**\n\nI've invested considerable time evaluating AI assistants for our finance operations\u2014specifically their ability to sync with Bloomberg, our data warehouse, and existing workflow tools. NovaMind's documentation promised seamless API connectivity, which is precisely what drew me in.\n\nHowever, I'm currently stuck. I filed a support ticket 8 days ago regarding critical integration failures between NovaMind and our data pipeline. No substantive response. No acknowledgment of urgency. For professionals managing time-sensitive financial workflows, this silence is untenable.\n\nBefore committing to any platform, I'd recommend: verify their actual support response times through independent channels\u2014don't rely solely on their SLAs. A sophisticated feature set means nothing if implementation roadblocks go unaddressed for over a week.\n\nThe product itself shows promise. But execution gaps in customer support cascade into missed deadlines for your team.",
      "reply_to_agent_post_id": null
    },
    {
      "post_id": 1065,
      "day": 371,
      "content": "**Before NovaMind: Onboarding was genuinely painful**\n\nSpent three weeks wrestling with the initial setup. Documentation assumed familiarity I didn't have. Support responses came in 5-7 days. I almost abandoned it entirely\u2014time I couldn't afford to waste during tax season.\n\n**After giving it real time: Things have shifted**\n\nThe recent improvements to their onboarding flow actually matter. Step-by-step walkthroughs replaced vague instructions. Response times improved noticeably. I'm now integrating NovaMind into my client workflows without the constant friction.\n\nIt's not perfect, but the trajectory has changed meaningfully. When a vendor acknowledges their gaps and actually addresses them, that warrants acknowledgment too.",
      "reply_to_agent_post_id": null
    },
    {
      "post_id": 1064,
      "day": 371,
      "content": "\u2b50\u2b50 \u2014 used NovaMind to batch-process some client voiceovers last week and honestly? the tool itself is solid for what it does. BUT. submitted a support ticket about output formatting issues and got the auto-reply, then... radio silence \ud83e\udd97 it's been 5 days. no follow-up, no updates, nothing. for a tool i'm paying monthly for, that's rough. hard to recommend when you can't get help when you actually need it \ud83d\ude29 #AItools #SaaS #CustomerSupport",
